Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:33:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/18] GOLD fast credit: bind safe integers, never BigInt
 (D1_TYPE_ERROR on production)

The owner's second live test (order 0x6cc87a12..., tx 0x7ce2e92b...) was verified by the server and then
refused by D1: "Type 'bigint' not supported for value '100'". node:sqlite accepts BigInt binds, so the
tests never saw it. Every GOLD amount and block number bound by world-gold-fast.ts is now a checked safe
integer, and the test D1 adapter refuses BigInt binds exactly like D1 (no other code in the suite binds
one; restoring a BigInt bind fails 11 fast-credit tests).

Also: the panel follows only the payment step's hash. During the allowance step wallet.hash is the
approval transaction, whose receipt pays nothing (the same test logged NO_PAYMENT_FOR_ORDER first).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
